@startuml c4-context

title Yóbbu — System Context (C4 Level 1)

skinparam defaultFontSize 10
skinparam backgroundColor #ffffff
skinparam ArrowColor #444444
skinparam ArrowThickness 1.2
skinparam NoteBackgroundColor #fffde7
skinparam NoteBorderColor #d0d0d0

skinparam actor {
  BackgroundColor #FFF9C4
  BorderColor #F9A825
  FontStyle bold
}
skinparam package {
  BackgroundColor #BBDEFB
  BorderColor #1565C0
  FontStyle bold
}
skinparam rectangle {
  BackgroundColor #F5F5F5
  BorderColor #9E9E9E
}

actor "Customer\n[Person]" as Customer
actor "Courier\n[Person]" as Courier
actor "Operator\n[Person]" as Operator

package "Yóbbu\n[Software System]" as Yobbu {
  note as YN
    Real-time delivery dispatch
    platform for African markets.
    Selects couriers, tracks deliveries
    live, notifies all parties.
  end note
}

rectangle "Keycloak\n[Identity Provider]\nOIDC + PKCE — manages accounts,\nroles and token issuance" as Keycloak
rectangle "Notification Channels\n[External System — simulated in V1]\nPush, SMS and email delivery" as Notif
rectangle "Map Tiles Provider\n[External System]\nOpenStreetMap-compatible raster tiles\n(self-hosted or CDN)" as Tiles

Customer --> Yobbu : places order, tracks delivery on map,\nreceives notifications, cancels, rates
Courier  --> Yobbu : reports availability and position,\naccepts / refuses offers, updates status
Operator --> Yobbu : monitors all deliveries on a map,\nresolves blocked cases, reads metrics

Yobbu --> Keycloak    : authenticates users (OIDC) ;\nfetches public keys to validate tokens
Yobbu --> Notif       : sends push, SMS and email\nnotifications to customers and couriers
Yobbu ..> Tiles       : fetches map tiles for the\nlive-tracking map (dotted = V1 TBD)

note right of Tiles
  ADR for tile provider to be written
  in phase 0.4 (1.4 in PLAN.md).
end note

note bottom of Yobbu
  The simulated merchant and the courier simulator
  are internal actors of the system, not external persons.
  They appear in the containers view (C4 Level 2).
end note

@enduml
